### Design Summary

| Aspect | Decision | Rationale |
|--------|----------|-----------|
| **Rule type** | `inventory_has` | Mine tasks → item ends up in inventory (preference order #1) |
| **Check item** | `flower_pot` | Breaking `potted_poppy` drops `flower_pot` + `poppy` separately; `potted_poppy` is never an inventory item |
| **Why `flower_pot` over `poppy`?** | No alternative source | Wild poppies could theoretically exist in the forest biome; `flower_pot` has zero natural sources |
| **Why not block removal?** | Coordinate dependency | `count_in_box_at_most` would require knowing absolute coords from spawn-relative offsets; `inventory_has` is simpler and more reliable |
| **Why single rule?** | Sufficiency | One `flower_pot` in inventory is both necessary and sufficient proof the potted poppy was mined in this scene |

